2. रुध् cl. 7. P. Ā. (Dhātup. xxix, 1) रुण॑द्धि, रुन्द्धे॑
(1. pl. -रुध्मस्, AV.;
रुन्धति, ˚ते, Br. &c.;
रोधति, MBh. pf. रुरोध, रुरुधे, RV. &c. &c.;
रुरुन्धतुः, MBh.;
aor. अरौत्, AV.;
अरौत्सीत्, Br. &c.;
रोत्सीस्, Up.;
अरुत्सि, अरुद्ध, Br.; Up.;
अरौत्सि, AitBr.;
अरोधम्, RV.;
अरुध्म, MaitrS.;
p. रुध॑त् cf. √ 1. रुध्;
अरुधत्, RV. &c. &c.;
Prec. रुध्यात्, Kāv.;
fut. रोद्धा Gr.;
रोत्स्यति, ˚ते, Br. &c. inf. रोद्धुम् or रोधितुम्, MBh.;
रोद्धोस्, Br.;
ind.p. रुद्ध्वा, MBh. &c.;
-रु॑ध्य, RV. &c. &c.;
-रुन्ध्य, MBh.;
-रु॑धम्, AV.; Br.;
-रु॑न्धम्, Br.;
-रो॑धम्, ib.),
to obstruct, check, arrest, stop, restrain, prevent, keep back, withhold, RV. (always with न), &c. &c.;
to avert, keep off, repel, Bhaṭṭ. (cf. रुधत् under √ 1. रुध्);
to shut, lock up, confine in (loc.), Mn.; MBh. &c. (accord. to Vop. also with double acc.);
to besiege, blockade, invest, Pat.; MBh. &c.;
to close, block up (a path), R.;
to cover, conceal, veil, obscure, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to stop up, fill, ib.;
to lay (dust), Ragh.;
to touch, move (the heart), Bālar.;
to torment, harass, R.;
to lose, be deprived of (acc.), TS.; ŚBr.;
to tear, rend asunder (?), AV. xix, 29, 3 :
Caus. रोधयति (ep. also ˚ते and रुन्धयति ; aor. अरूरुधत्; Pass. रोध्यते),
to stop, arrest, MBh.;
to cause to be confined by (acc.), Pañcar.;
to cause to be besieged by (instr.), Ragh.;
to close (with a cover or lid), Bhpr.;
to fetter, enchain, influence, BhP.;
to oppress, torment, harass, MBh.; R. :
Desid. रोरुत्सते (Br.), ˚ति (MBh.), to wish to obstruct &c.:
Intens. रोरुध्यते, रोरोद्धि, to obstruct intensely or repeatedly &c. Gr. (only रोरुधः, R. ii, 58, 20.)
